# How to Run the UnEncrypted Chat Server and Client
====================================================
This guide explains how to compile and run the Chat Server and Chat Client included in this project. 
It also lists any passwords used by the system so administrators are aware of them.


# Requirements
===============
- Java 8 or higher
- A Java‑capable IDE (IntelliJ, Eclipse, VS Code) OR command‑line tools
- The project source files from this repository


# Running the Server
=====================
1) Open the project in your IDE or navigate to the source directory in a terminal.

2) Locate and run the following files:

- ChatServer.java
``` javac ChatServer.java ```
``` java ChatServer ```

3) When launched, the server will prompt for:

- IP Address to bind to
Use 0.0.0.0 to listen on all interfaces (This is your local host, used for testing)

- Port number
Default: 5050

4) The Server Control Panel will appear, showing:

- Server log output
- Active user list
- Buttons for saving logs, stopping the server, and kicking users

The server begins listening immediately after startup.


# Running the Client
=====================

1) Locate and run:

- ChatClientGUI
``` java ChatClientGUI.java ```
``` javac ChatClientGUI ```

2) The client will prompt for:

- Server host (must match the server)
- Server port (must match the server)
- Display name

3) After connecting, the client window will show:

- Incoming messages
- Your own sent messages
- Any server notifications


# Admin Features
=================

- Kick User Command (Client Side)
Users with admin access can initiate a kick request by typing:

``` /kickuser ```

The client will prompt for the admin password.
The admin password is hard‑coded in the client:

``` admin123 ```

This password is required to request the active user list and initiate a kick action.


# Kick User (Server Side)
==========================

The server GUI includes a Kick User button that allows the administrator to select and remove a connected user.


# Server Shutdown Behavior
===========================

When the server is stopped (via the GUI or window close):

- All clients receive a SERVER_SHUTDOWN command.
- Clients display a shutdown countdown window.
- Clients exit automatically after the countdown.


# Notes
========
- This version of the chat system is unencrypted and intended for LAN or educational use.
- The server must be running before any clients attempt to connect.
- All passwords are hardcoded.
